check_jacobi_fold_width_is_pinned OK (IDENTICAL): K_LIB_JACOBI_EIGH resolves to 32/32/32 (Apple/NVIDIA/AMD) against the identity floor's 32; this build compiles against 32, a power of two. NOTE: 32 threads is HALF an AMD CDNA wavefront -- under IDENTICAL the halving tree touches only the 32 slots real threads wrote, so that is a scheduling question there and not a numeric one.
check_jacobi_fold_shape OK (IDENTICAL): device fold == host halving tree bit for bit at width 32 (bits 1266679831 ), and the fixture separates that shape from a sequential fold ( 16777262.0 vs 16777278.0 ). The library fold on THIS device was NOT INSTANTIABLE at this width (block size must exceed the lane width; DEVIATION 528), so no comparison was taken
