check_jacobi_device_sizes OK: 16, 32, 33, 64, 128, 256 all satisfy A V = V diag(lambda) and V^T V = I. The 32-feature cap is gone.
check_jacobi_reaches_past_32 OK: top eigenvalue 9.598471641540527 -> 1001.3273315429688 for a +1000 spike at index 63 (past the old cap), and -> 1006.0556640625 for the same spike at index 5 (inside it). Both move, so the kernel reads the whole matrix.
check_jacobi_scale_invariance OK: A and 1000 A both converge in 7.0 sweeps to relative off-diagonal 3.129391927883529e-12 and 3.0815703721404075e-12, and the spectra agree to 3.935608404764001e-07 after dividing out the scale
check_jacobi_is_a_pure_function_of_its_input OK (IDENTICAL): n = 33 -- all 2178 output cells bit-identical to a host Float32 replay of the same partials, the same halving fold and the same pinned rotation, in 6 sweeps. Every pin in the kernel is REACHED.
check_jacobi_sweep_count_is_a_knife_edge OK (IDENTICAL): n = 64, tol bits 877130934 -> 877130935 (ONE ulp, 1.8622345e-07 -> 1.8622346e-07, found in 28 probes) moves the executed sweeps 7 -> 6 and with them 1325 of 4096 eigenvector cells, worst |delta| 1.9194558262825012e-06, worst eigenvalue |delta| 0.0. A last-bit difference in the exit quantity is NOT a last-bit difference in the answer. Repeat runs at a fixed tolerance are bit-identical.
check_jacobi_fold_shape_decides_the_sweep_count OK (IDENTICAL): n = 32, seed 1. The halving fold changes its mind at tol bits 853093745 and a sequential fold at 853093746. At tol = 2.528279e-08 the two shapes execute 6 and 7 sweeps ON THE SAME INPUT, and their eigenvectors then differ in 190 of 1024 cells, worst |delta| 1.341104507446289e-06. The device (sweeps = 6) takes the halving shape. THAT is why the fold is not a library call any more.
check_jacobi_denormal_exit_test OK (IDENTICAL): the device converged at sweep 0 on an 8 x 8 matrix whose exit test is entirely denormal, and returned it untouched. The same numbers unflushed on this host give limit = 2.205718e-39 (denormal) and 2*off = 1.3166577e-37 over 28 denormal squares, so a denormal-honoring backend would run its whole 15-sweep budget instead and return a DIFFERENT matrix. That is the discrete consequence row 10's ftz aligns; it is one compare, not a last bit.
check_jacobi_reports_the_sweep_cap OK (IDENTICAL): the fixture converges in 7 sweeps; capped at 2 the kernel reports converged = 0, sweeps = 2 and a relative off-diagonal of 0.27800614, and its eigenvectors are 0.6270713657140732 away from the converged ones at the worst cell. Both callers RAISE on that flag in both modes, which is the deviation from RAFT's Jacobi arm recorded in DEVIATION BLOCK 2.
